There's been lots of discussion about features that should be added/removed
from the game, the main ones being:

	1) Polypiling: Some of us think we should put some restrictions on
	   it, while the other half think we should leave it alone.
	2) Choking on food: Some of us think it's a really stupid way to die
	   and that nobody should ever choke, while the other half think
	   that if you choke that's your tough luck.
	3) Drowning: Some think there should be "Really enter the pool of
	   water" prompts, while the other half think that we should all
	   be more careful.
	4) Attacking monsters: Some of us think there should be "Really
	   attack the floating eye/acid blob" prompts while the other half
	   think that that's your tough luck for running through the dungeon
	   so fast.

Now, we've all heard the arguments for and against all of them a zillion times,
and THEY'RE NOT GOING TO GO AWAY. We all have our opinions and they're probably
not going to change. Therefore my proposal is:

Have a few more compile time options that one can set, with the default options
being, say, the way things are currently, but which can be set to configure the
game to the way an individual person installing nethack likes it:

/* #define HARDPOLYPILE /* Only polymorph top 10 objects in a polypile */
/* #define HARDCONFLICT /* Ring of conflict only affects monsters 50% time */
/* #define SAFEEAT      /* Player barfs instead of chokes */
/* #define SAFEPOOL     /* Player prompted with "really enter pool of water" */
/* #define SAFEMONST    /* Player prompted before hitting floating eyes */

This way, those who don't like certain features can easily change them
to their own personal whims, with the change being "real" for their
system as opposed to the "if you don't like it don't do it/be more
careful solutions". Those who have modem or line noise may want to set
the last two options, while nethack purists may want to set the first
two. To each his or her own...

